Z||000000||Brian84SE||02-17-2000||08:46 PM||||I failed emissions(High oxides of Nitrogen).  Checked EGR, defective, so I replaced.(Along with some vacuum lines).<BR>Failed again! Although NO was 200ppm lower this time. Not getting any codes from the ECM. The paper they give you says "possibly computer sensors or probably oxygen sensor"<BR>Any comments folks? (this is a 4cyl. by the way)||||reg||1
Z||000001||fiero56||02-17-2000||09:02 PM||||If NOx  was under, I would check the O2 sensor. Also, how old/what kind of shape is the catylitic convertor in. Might just be time for a new one.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Brian84SE||02-17-2000||09:58 PM||||Catalytic is original. (90,000 miles).  Original NOX reading was 2200. After EGR change was 1900.  My state has a max of 1400.||||reg||1
Z||000003||88formula||02-17-2000||10:04 PM||||Change the O2 sensor and put some fuel injector cleaner in it and it will pass if the cat is doing its job.||||reg||1
Z||000004||mwbackus||02-17-2000||10:28 PM||||90,000 mile on a cat is about 40,000 over the intended duration.  Replace it, it is probably clogged a bit anyway.  The old honeycomb design cats are not even worth using, even if they are still working.  Much has changed over 15 yrs, and the newer designs flow much better.  The best freeflow cat I have found for the $$ is made by Catco, they are available from Summit for around $50.<P>Mike||||reg||1
